WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.045
Week 34: Pan-Hispanic Variation and Dialect Listening. recognize major regional forms ask for clarification without judgment adapt address and vocabulary

2
00:00:11.045 --> 00:00:19.977
Form and meaning. Tú, vos, usted, and vosotros systems; leísmo recognition; lexical variation; code-switching and register.

3
00:00:19.977 --> 00:00:46.470
Model set. ¿Vos tenés tiempo mañana? Vosotros podéis entrar por aquí. Ustedes esperan la guagua en esa esquina. En México, camión puede significar autobús. No entendí esa palabra; ¿qué significa aquí? Do you have time tomorrow? You all can enter here. You all wait for the bus on that corner. In Mexico, camión can mean bus. I did not understand that word; what does it mean here?

4
00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:56.600
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:11.530
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: recognize major regional forms; ask for clarification without judgment; adapt address and vocabulary. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:38.748
Model language. ¿Vos tenés tiempo mañana? — Do you have time tomorrow? Vosotros podéis entrar por aquí. — You all can enter here. Ustedes esperan la guagua en esa esquina. — You all wait for the bus on that corner. En México, camión puede significar autobús. — In Mexico, camión can mean bus. No entendí esa palabra; ¿qué significa aquí? — I did not understand that word; what does it mean here?

7
00:01:38.748 --> 00:01:48.497
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
